 "slug": "ep123-sorry-shrink",
 "title": "Every SORRY Here Costs An Inch ☕",
 "made_for_kids": false,
 "premise": "In a town where every sorry shrinks you an inch, my aunt Mae is the size of a mug, and everyone says she is the politest woman alive. Every Sunday I play her at cards on her sun porch, and I have lost sixty games in a row.",
 "twist": "She is not polite, she is the town's unbeaten card player: every inch she lost went on the sorry she says each time she lays down a winning hand. When I finally beat her I say sorry out of habit, and I shrink an inch.",
